# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 3: Graph 3-coloring (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"
msgstr "Exemplo 3: Coloração de grafo com 3 cores (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Max-$k$-Cut problem partitions the vertices of a graph into $k$ groups to maximize the number of edges whose endpoints belong to different groups. For $k = 3$ this is equivalent to finding a 3-coloring that maximizes cross-color edges.\n"
msgstr "O problema Max-$k$-Cut particiona os vértices de um grafo em $k$ grupos para maximizar o número de arestas cujos extremos pertencem a grupos diferentes. Para $k = 3$, isso equivale a encontrar uma coloração de 3 cores que maximize as arestas entre cores diferentes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, assign each node $i \\in V$ to one of $k$ groups with binary variables $x_{i,c}$ for color $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. The one-hot constraint $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ for each node enforces a unique assignment. The objective maximizes cross-group edges:\n"
msgstr "Formalmente, atribua cada nó $i \\in V$ a um dos $k$ grupos com variáveis binárias $x_{i,c}$ para a cor $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. A restrição one-hot $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ para cada nó impõe uma atribuição única. O objetivo maximiza as arestas entre grupos diferentes:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The one-hot constraints are ideal for XY-mixers, which the optimizer handles natively.\n"
msgstr "As restrições one-hot são ideais para mixers XY, que o otimizador trata de forma nativa.\n"

